In `CreateOrUpdateDevice`, the device-limit check is implemented as a separate `CountDevices(...)` call followed by a later insert/upsert path when `count < s.deviceLimit`:

```go
count, err := s.CountDevices(...)
...
if count >= s.deviceLimit {
  return s.updateDevice(ctx, device)
}
// else proceeds to INSERT/UPSERT
```

Because the count and the subsequent write are not performed atomically (no transaction/lock/unique constraint-based enforcement shown in this diff), concurrent requests can both observe `count` below the limit and both insert, exceeding the configured device limit (classic T

